This is one of those times I really wish Steam gave a third option for a review, an in-the-middle "meh" option, though since I'm absolutely forced to choose one, I'd barely, and I mean BARELY err on the side of recommended.
Long story short is that this is a 'fair' megaman clone.  Nothing special or unique, and not very long, but not really that *bad* either.  There are positives, though for each positive there's a counterbalance;
- The graphics are not bad at all, evoking a kind of 16-bit Megaman feel, and the character designs are pretty cute, but there's nothing that really stands out;
- The music is quite good, sometimes rather great even, but most the game uses a singular motif that can get tiring, and the sound effects are stock trash (with especially bad mini voice clips in the cutscenes);
- The story is... okay, servicable for this type of game, but the Engish translation and even the formatting of the text in the boxes is embarrassingly bad;
- The gameplay overall is fine, and satisfying enough for a Megaman fan, but there are some very annoying aspects such as even your default pea shooter taking ammo and shooting only in three-round bursts for some reason (though these problems are SLIGHTLY alleviated via the hidden powerups you can find).
There's also a weird lack of polish that I feel somewhat bothered by, with things like very swift screen transitions with no boss intro or 'got a weapon' outro to the stages, and how SOME dialogue scenes are skippable while others aren't.  It's also a painfully short game, with four challenging, but quick normal stages each with eactly 1 hidden powerup, followed by 4 'fortress' stages, and that's it, that's the whole game.  Very cut and dry.
Still, though, all things considered, and especially with the price being so low frankly, for a Megaman fan this just barely,
makes the cut to be worth checking out, especially with the promise of more content such as various playable characters later on.  All things considered though, if you're looking for a good Megaman fangame where you play as a girl, you'd do better checking out Rosenkreuzstilette, Rokko Chan or MegaMari.

