The Pros:
- Very fun fighting with a nice variety of moves (Reminded me of a brawler called Urban Reign published by Namco for PS2);
- Interesting story providing a nice atmosphere along with the bright and colorful Hong Kong (Besides the whole "Gang/Mafia Wars VS Undercover Cop" concept that isn't exactly original);
The Cons:
- Beautiful but relatively small city (Compared to Series like Grand Theft Auto and Saints Row) and with limited interation (There aren't many interactive places enter/explore) and quite linear mission structure;
- Oversimplified vehicles control (They don't fell "unique" in handling besides speed diferences and aren't much responsive to Physics);
- Limited weapons handling, numbers and variety, no customization;
Recently some concepts about a cancelled sequel has been seen on many gaming websites (Along with the also on limbo Alan Wake 2). Just the idea of  sequel to this game with a co-op mode just amaze me. Sadly, with the United Front Games officially closing down, its unlike but there is still a possibility considering that Sleeping Dogs is  a rehash of True Crime: Hong Kong brought by Square Enix from Activision back in 2011.

The world is too much with us; late and soon,
Getting and spending, we lay waste our powers;
Little we see in Nature that is ours;
We have given our hearts away, a sordid boon!
This Sea that bares her bosom to the moon;
The winds that will be howling at all hours,
And are up-gathered now like sleeping flowers,
For this, for everything, we are out of tune;
It moves us not.—Great God! I’d rather be
A pagan suckled in a creed outworn;
So might I, standing on this pleasant lea,
Have glimpses that would make me less forlorn;
Have sight of Proteus rising from the sea;
Or hear old Triton blow his wreathèd horn.

